 4. 🤖 Exclusive: Main Street&#x27;s budget AI boom 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Goldman Sachs. Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Small businesses across America are embracing AI, but usage and spending vary dramatically by state, Axios' Herb Scribner writes from an exclusive Goldman Sachs survey of 2,474 small business owners. 

 Why it matters: Companies nationwide, big and small, are figuring out how best to incorporate AI into their workforces and what that means for productivity. 🧮 By the numbers: For all the talk about AI's explosive growth in the enterprise, the survey shows 73% of small businesses are spending $100 or less per month on AI.

 In Texas, most use AI for marketing copy. In Florida, it's mainly for productivity. More data . 

 
 
